// POLYFIT - least squares (or exact) polynomial fit with a Vandermonde matrix.
// Data: x values in L1, y values in L2.
// Out: [E] = Vandermonde matrix (columns 1, x, x^2, ...), [C] = coefficients a0..aD
//      y = a0 + a1 x + ... + aD x^D
ClrHome
Disp "POLY FIT, X IN L1","Y IN L2"
Input "DEGREE? ",O
dim(L₁)→G
{G,O+1}→dim([E])
For(I,1,G)
1→[E](I,1)
For(J,2,O+1)
L₁(I)^(J-1)→[E](I,J)
End
End
List►matr(L₂,[F])
augment([E]ᵀ*[E],[E]ᵀ*[F])→[J]
0→S
0→Q
O+1→W
prgmZRREF
{O+1,1}→dim([C])
Fill(0,[C])
For(I,1,R)
[J](I,O+2)→[C](ʟPIV(I),1)
End
ClrHome
If R<O+1
Disp "NOT UNIQUE (TOO FEW","POINTS), ONE SOLUTION:"
Disp "Y=A0+A1X+...+ADX^D","[A0,...,AD] = [C]"
Pause [C]►Frac
